        <groundspeak:log id="684650900">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP348 Dove of Hope &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was our only failed search of the day.  Construction had taken over our planned parking spot but stopping there we could see that the hill where we should be headed had a large area fenced off.  If we'd both been feeling better we might have gone closer to see if the cap was accessible but we decided to find a shady spot and have lunch instead.  Once home and reading gumbyphv's note that the cap was in fact inside the fencing it turned out to be the right choice.  It's a great spot, though, and hopefully the cap won't be destroyed by the construction and we can come back another time.  Thanks anyway.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682475488">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4853503">gumbyphv</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;Where the construction helped me at the last cap it definitely didn't help me at BCP348 Dove of Hope.  I walked to the cap and got close, unfortunately not close enough.  I could see the manhole cover that housed the cap but it was on the wrong side of a construction fence.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
